    "result": "The fix is complete and verified. Here's what I did:\n\n**Problem**: The `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` file because the `--ci` flag was being consumed by the top-level `frai` command parser instead of being passed through to the `frai-gate` subcommand.\n\n**Root Cause**: The top-level `frai` command defines `--ci` as an option (line 605), so Commander's parser captures it at the top level. This prevented it from reaching the `gate` subcommand's handler.\n\n**Solution**: Modified the `gate` command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to extract arguments directly from `process.argv` (starting from where 'gate' appears) instead of relying on Commander's parsed arguments. This ensures all flags, including `--ci`, are passed unchanged to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Verification**: Successfully tested with `node packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci` and confirmed both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created correctly.",
